      "sourceTextSha256": "0928d931e6c20b71b7c9c7df6cbe5d05aa647dfc788e811e5e10ecc701efbc7b",
      "text": "Breakfast. Meet your guide in the hotel lobby.\n\nExcursion to Corcovado Mountain and the Christ the Redeemer statue (4 hours) with a  guide.\n\nArrival at the station, where we take a special open, eco-friendly train through the jungle to the top of Corcovado Hill. On both sides of the road, you’ll see the breathtaking views of Tijuca Forest. At the top of Corcovado Hill, 710 meters above sea level, stands the symbol of Rio—the Christ the Redeemer statue (38 meters tall), erected in 1931. From the observation deck, you’ll enjoy a stunning panorama of the metropolis and its surroundings: the bridge to Niterói, Guanabara Bay, the Botanical Garden, the world’s largest stadium Maracanã, Sugarloaf Mountain, and much more.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "word_exact",
        "fileId": "1cf7wueRDIZK0ocnEAfXaDl1_yBCdjFNh",
        "documentSha256": "41f369baf395231c6d90ef1b3b1f76b6222a6a8eda59a301c61a48727be5e51a",
